00:32:19,567 --> 00:32:22,067
我们这儿向来半点排场都不给。
We tend not to give you any.

676
00:32:22,067 --> 00:32:23,767
其实我还挺喜欢那些排场的。
Well, I do like the trappings
of show business.

677
00:32:23,800 --> 00:32:26,700
-哦，你喜欢啊？那我道歉。
-是啊，你们这儿还真是一点排场都没给我。
-Oh, do you? I apologise.
-Yeah, you certainly
haven't given me any.

678
00:32:26,733 --> 00:32:27,933
-真没有。
-（观众笑声）
-No.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

679
00:32:27,967 --> 00:32:29,467
特别是那个空调，简直绝了。
It's the air-conditioning,
the worst thing.

680
00:32:29,500 --> 00:32:31,233
后台都在说，里面冻得跟冰窖似的。
Well, they're saying
it's like cold inside there.

681
00:32:31,267 --> 00:32:33,933
我刚才就是想去洗个手。
你见识过这儿的厕所没？
I just wanted to go
and have a wash.
Have you seen the khazi here?

682
00:32:33,967 --> 00:32:35,933
见识过了，我本指望
你用不着去那儿呢。
Yeah, I was hoping you
wouldn't need that.

683
00:32:35,967 --> 00:32:37,800
可不是嘛……我根本没敢用。
No, well... I didn't use it.

684
00:32:39,700 --> 00:32:41,400
你可是个伦敦东区硬汉。
You are an East End boy.

685
00:32:41,433 --> 00:32:43,933
没错。我打西汉姆的
普莱斯托出来的。
Yeah, I am. I'm out of
Plaistow in West Ham.

686
00:32:43,967 --> 00:32:45,733
想必当年跟你一起
念书的那帮哥们儿，
Presumably, half
the people you were
at school with

687
00:32:45,767 --> 00:32:47,600
有一半都在局子里蹲着吧。再过不久……
are all in clink. Shortly...

688
00:32:47,633 --> 00:32:50,533
倒也没有。我是说，
当年跟我一起练拳击的
那帮小伙子里，
No, not really. I mean,
there's a lot of boys
we used to go boxing with.

689
00:32:50,567 --> 00:32:52,133
有一个叫托尼·马钱特，
One of them is
Tony Marchant,

690
00:32:52,167 --> 00:32:53,800
现在可是全英国数一数二
的大编剧呢。
who's one of the top
writers in this country,
you know.

691
00:32:53,833 --> 00:32:56,067
还有格伦·墨菲，
现在当了演员，你看，其实……
There's Glen Murphy,
who's an actor,
you know, so there's...

692
00:32:56,100 --> 00:32:59,067
我都忘了你还练过拳击。
你当年是不是代表英格兰打过比赛？
I forgotten you did boxing.
Didn't you box for England?

693
00:32:59,067 --> 00:33:01,867
算是代表英格兰打过
新手级的比赛吧。
I boxed kind of
at the novice level
for England.

694
00:33:01,900 --> 00:33:03,933
跟威尔士队交手过几次。
I boxed against Wales
a couple of times.

695
00:33:03,967 --> 00:33:05,833
-你一共打过多少场？
-八十八场。
-How many fights did you have?
-Eighty-eight.

696
00:33:05,867 --> 00:33:08,567
-八十八场？
-对。赢了一场。没错。
-Eighty-eight?
-Yeah. I won one. Yeah.

697
00:33:08,600 --> 00:33:10,533
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

698
00:33:10,567 --> 00:33:13,667
那你到底是怎么从东区练拳击
So how did you get
from kind of East End boxing

699
00:33:13,700 --> 00:33:17,067
这整套行当，转行去戏剧学院的？
that whole thing,
to a drama school?

700
00:33:17,067 --> 00:33:19,667
哎，我爸妈当年搬出了普莱斯托，
Well, my mum and dad,
they moved out
of Plaistow

701
00:33:19,700 --> 00:33:21,500
因为我爸是倒腾水果生意的。
'cause Dad was in
the fruit game.

702
00:33:21,533 --> 00:33:25,400
他们搬到了埃德蒙顿、恩菲尔德那一带，
And they moved to Edmonton,
Enfield, around that area,

703
00:33:25,433 --> 00:33:27,500
我就在那边念书，还参演了学校的话剧。
and I went to school there
and done the school play.

704
00:33:27,533 --> 00:33:30,600
我觉得我妈看了以后琢磨着：
“这小子有正经出路了，”
Which I think, my mum
looked at and thought,
"There's a way for him out,"

705
00:33:30,633 --> 00:33:33,200
你懂的，省得成天在外面惹是生非什么的，
you know, no getting
into trouble and all that
sort of stuff

706
00:33:33,233 --> 00:33:35,133
于是她把我送进了戏剧学院，当时……
and she put me
in a drama school,
which I...

707
00:33:35,167 --> 00:33:37,100
我自己也挺想去的，我在那儿撑了一年。
I wanted to do and
I lasted a year there.

708
00:33:37,133 --> 00:33:38,767
你是因为什么被开除的？
What did you get expelled for?

709
00:33:38,800 --> 00:33:42,900
哎，演艺圈里势利眼可多着呢，
杰里米，呃……
Well, there's a lot
of snobbery in my game,
Jeremy, um...

710
00:33:42,933 --> 00:33:45,733
我觉得在他们眼里，
我对其他小孩算是个危险分子。
And I was looked at, I think,
as a bit of a danger
to the other kids.

711
00:33:45,767 --> 00:33:48,500
我是说，在我上正音课纠正口音之前，
你真该听听我那时候说话的德行。
I mean, before I had elocution
lessons, you should've
heard me.

712
00:33:48,533 --> 00:33:50,267
-真的吗？
-（观众大笑）
-Really?
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

713
00:33:50,300 --> 00:33:52,400
我那时候就是个小痞子，你懂吧？
I was a bit
of a toe rag, you know?

714
00:33:52,433 --> 00:33:54,867
-不至于吧！
-而且我还破坏过一辆车。
-No!
-And I sabotaged a car.

715
00:33:54,900 --> 00:33:56,433
-我把图钉按进……
-谁的车？
-I put tacks in...
-Whose?

716
00:33:56,467 --> 00:33:58,433
女校长的。
The headmistress.

717
00:33:58,467 --> 00:34:01,067
-后来被西伦敦来的家伙给告发了，不用想都知道……
-把图钉扎轮胎里？
-And I got grassed by someone
from West London, obviously...
-Tacks in the tyres?

718
00:34:01,067 --> 00:34:04,067
-又是西伦敦！
-对。然后我就被学校轰出去了。
-West London!
-Yeah. And I was
thrown out the school.

719
00:34:04,067 --> 00:34:06,200
不过现在回头想想，开除得一点没错。
But looking back at it,
quite rightly so, you know.

720
00:34:06,233 --> 00:34:09,133
-搞不好真会出人命的，不是吗？
-嗯哼。
-Could've been a dangerous
thing, couldn't it?
-Mmm-hmm.

721
00:34:10,067 --> 00:34:11,333
行吧，好歹你现在说话
挺像模像样了。
Well, at least you talk
proper now.

722
00:34:11,367 --> 00:34:13,200
-那可不，挺得体的。
-这就成，关键就在这儿。
-Yeah, I do.
-That's the important thing.

723
00:34:13,233 --> 00:34:15,633
-我现在算是个正经演员了，
对吧？
-对，一点没错。
-I'm a proper actor now,
aren't I?
-Yeah, well, exactly.

724
00:34:15,667 --> 00:34:17,367
-可你老演恶棍大反派。
-我才没有。
-You always play a villain.
-I don't.

725
00:34:17,400 --> 00:34:19,900
得了吧，我是说，亨利八世
可就是个恶棍。
Well, I mean, Henry VIII,
he was a villain.

726
00:34:19,933 --> 00:34:22,400
亨利八世搞不好是
有史以来
最大的黑帮头子。
Henry VIII was probably
the biggest gangster
there'd ever been.

727
00:34:22,433 --> 00:34:25,733
是他把英格兰造就成
今天这个样子的。
He made England
what it is today.

728
00:34:25,767 --> 00:34:27,333
这功劳
我宁愿算在伊丽莎白一世头上。
I'd have
Elizabeth I for that one.

729
00:34:27,367 --> 00:34:29,633
-行吧，你知道的，我是说
太了不起了……
-一脉相承嘛。
-Well, you know, I mean,
fantastic...
-Same stock.

730
00:34:29,667 --> 00:34:32,400
嗨，你知道的，那可是我闺女，
爱死她了。
她是个正派人。
Well, you know, it was my kid,
loved her.
She's proper.

731
00:34:32,433 --> 00:34:34,133
（观众笑声）
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

732
00:34:34,167 --> 00:34:36,733
你以前是不是在鲜花市场干过？
是鲜花市场吧？
Didn't you used to work
in the flower market?
Was it the flower market?

733
00:34:36,767 --> 00:34:39,833
不是，是水果市场。
我和我爸在斯皮塔佛德干过。
No, the fruit market. I worked
in Spitalfields with my dad.

734
00:34:39,867 --> 00:34:41,600
我爸以前是个菜贩子。
My dad was a greengrocer.

735
00:34:41,633 --> 00:34:43,467
-我还以为你爸开出租车呢。
-不是，他现在才是出租车司机。
-I thought your dad was
a cab driver.
-No, he's a cab driver now.

736
00:34:43,500 --> 00:34:46,267
关于他有个极逗的事儿。
你知道的，那种出租车司机的段子，懂吧？
There's a great story
about him. You know,
cab driver stories, right?

737
00:34:46,300 --> 00:34:49,800
我从没觉得我爸是个好糊弄的人，
但这回他真信了这个邪。
I never looked at my dad
as being gullible
but he stood for this one.

738
00:34:49,833 --> 00:34:52,633
他说，“可不嘛……”
我们当时站在酒吧里，
他正跟我讲这事儿：
And he says, "Yeah..."
We're standing in the pub
and he's telling me this story

739
00:34:52,667 --> 00:34:55,700
说是有天有个家伙
从多切斯特酒店走出来，
about this fella who came out
of the Dorchester one day

740
00:34:55,733 --> 00:34:57,433
拦了辆出租车，
司机问，
and hailed a cab
and the taxi said,

741
00:34:57,467 --> 00:34:59,500
“你想去哪儿？”
那人说：“柏林。”
"Where do you want to go?"
And he said, "Berlin."

742
00:34:59,533 --> 00:35:01,467
他说：“我赶不上飞机了，过不去。
我必须去柏林。
He said, "I've missed the
flights. I can't get there.
I need to go to Berlin.

743
00:35:01,500 --> 00:35:03,367
“我要你把我送到多佛港，上轮渡。
齐活。
"I want you to take me
down to Dover, on the boat.
Bosh.

744
00:35:03,400 --> 00:35:06,167
“穿过法国，把我送到柏林。
我必须赶过去。”
"Go through France,
take me to Berlin.
I need to get there."

745
00:35:06,200 --> 00:35:08,167
结果那出租车司机还真照办了。
So the cab driver done that.

746
00:35:08,200 --> 00:35:11,500
等开到了柏林，把那家伙放下时，
对方全给的现钞，
And he's got to Berlin, and as
he dropped the fella off
he's paid him in readies,

747
00:35:11,533 --> 00:35:14,267
就在那司机
刚准备调头
打道回府的时候，
and as the cab
driver was about
to turn away and come home,

748
00:35:14,300 --> 00:35:16,267
有个哥们儿
从酒店里跑出来说：
a fella came
out of the hotel and said,

749
00:35:16,300 --> 00:35:18,300
“师傅，能把我
捎回伦敦吗？”
"Mate, can you take me
to London?"

750
00:35:20,167 --> 00:35:21,733
我爸居然真信了这鬼话！
And my dad believed that.

751
00:35:21,767 --> 00:35:23,700
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

752
00:35:23,733 --> 00:35:26,200
-对啊。
-咱们还是聊聊车吧，成吗？
-Yeah.
-Let's talk about cars, okay?

753
00:35:27,067 --> 00:35:29,067
你是个捷豹死忠粉，对吧？
You're a Jag man, yeah?

754
00:35:29,100 --> 00:35:32,267
其实我从来没对车
那么痴狂过。
I've never been really that
mad on cars.

755
00:35:32,300 --> 00:35:34,700
我这辈子开的向来都是破烂货，呃……
I've always had old bangers
all my life and, uh...

756
00:35:34,733 --> 00:35:38,300
但在我小时候，那个年代的
终极神车
就是捷豹E-Type。
But as a kid, the car
at the time
was the E-Type Jag.

757
00:35:38,333 --> 00:35:41,067
-现在也是。
-嗨，你知道的，
那简直是件神物。
-It still is.
-Well, you know,
it's a fantastic tool.

758
00:35:41,067 --> 00:35:44,367
-因为在当年，
E-Type真是个漂亮尤物。
-确实。
-'Cause in the past,
the E-Type was a pretty thing.
-Yeah.

759
00:35:44,400 --> 00:35:47,500
但它们身上总带着点阿瑟·戴利那种匪气，你懂的……
But they still have
that Arthur Daley, you know...

760
00:35:47,533 --> 00:35:49,233
捷豹嘛，妥妥的劫匪跑路车。
It's a getaway car, a Jag.

761
00:35:49,267 --> 00:35:52,167
我觉得也是。
这车一直自带
那种性感劲儿，对吧？
Well, I think so.
It's always had
that sexiness about it, innit?

762
00:35:52,200 --> 00:35:55,200
就是说啊，后座上——
-还得穿件克龙比大衣。体面的羊毛大衣之类。
I know, exactly. In the back.
-Crombies. Nice Crombie
and all that.

763
00:35:55,233 --> 00:35:56,733
对，后备箱里还得塞满赃物。
Yeah, the swag in the boot.

764
00:35:56,767 --> 00:35:58,467
这事儿我一直想不通，因为……
I can never work
that one out because

765
00:35:58,500 --> 00:36:00,267
我家附近
有一座驼峰桥，
near where I live,
there's a humpback bridge

766
00:36:00,300 --> 00:36:03,200
跨过一个车站，
桥面拱得特别厉害，知道吧？
that goes over a station,
which is quite humpy,
all right?

767
00:36:03,233 --> 00:36:05,433
我哥们儿不知道这茬，
当时正开着我的老捷豹，
And my mate didn't know,
he was driving my old Jag,

768
00:36:05,467 --> 00:36:07,867
我们直接飞跃
那座驼峰桥，
and we went flying
over the humpback

769
00:36:07,900 --> 00:36:09,833
底盘“轰”地砸在地上，车就熄火了。
and it hit the floor
and it switched off.

770
00:36:09,867 --> 00:36:11,700
整辆车彻底断电熄火了。
The whole car switched off.

771
00:36:11,733 --> 00:36:13,333
后面正好跟着辆厢型车，
开车的刚好是我熟人。
There was a fellow following
us behind in a van who
I happened to know.

772
00:36:13,367 --> 00:36:15,900
他问：“怎么回事？”
我说：“他把车给搞趴窝了。”
He said, "What's the matter?"
I said, "He's killed the car."

773
00:36:15,933 --> 00:36:19,233
他说：“没那么严重。”
他说：“捷豹车底有个按钮，
He said, "No, he ain't."
He said, "There's a button
at the bottom of a Jag

774
00:36:19,267 --> 00:36:21,967
-是个断电安全开关。
要是出了车祸……
-对。
-"and it's a switch-off thing.
So if you have a crash...
-Yeah.

775
00:36:22,067 --> 00:36:23,233
“……它就会自动断电。”
"...it switches itself off."

776
00:36:23,267 --> 00:36:25,567
这设计对银行劫匪可太不友好了。
Which is no good if
you're a bank robber.

777
00:36:25,600 --> 00:36:27,700
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

778
00:36:27,733 --> 00:36:29,467
确实不友好，对吧？
你想想……
It ain't, is it?
I mean...

779
00:36:29,500 --> 00:36:32,567
你正以一百英里时速狂飙，
条子紧贴在你屁股后头，
You're in a 100-mile chase
with the old bill
up your backsides,

780
00:36:32,600 --> 00:36:35,600
结果不小心磕了下路沿什么的，
车子啪一下断电熄火了，
and you happen to hit the kerb
or something and
the car switches off,

781
00:36:35,633 --> 00:36:36,933
那你可真就彻底玩完了。
you're really in trouble.

782
00:36:38,633 --> 00:36:40,667
言归正传，你的圈速跑得怎样？
Anyway, your lap. How was it?

783
00:36:40,700 --> 00:36:42,133
噢，爽翻了。
Oh, I loved it.

784
00:36:42,167 --> 00:36:44,700
其实我平时
开车并不快。
And I'm not
a fast driver, really.

785
00:36:44,733 --> 00:36:46,167
毕竟平时总得接送孩子。
'Cause I'm driving
the kids about.

786
00:36:46,200 --> 00:36:48,800
跟着斯提格在赛道上跑，
他教得真挺不错的。
And going around with Stig,
he's a really good teacher.

787
00:36:48,833 --> 00:36:50,500
-我是说……
-每个人都这么夸他。
-I mean...
-Everybody says that.

788
00:36:50,533 --> 00:36:52,267
只要你肯听他的。
你必须得听他的指点。
As long as you listen
to him. You've got
to listen to the guy.

789
00:36:52,300 --> 00:36:54,767
说实话，
到最后我都跑上瘾了。
And really,
in the end I was loving it.

790
00:36:54,800 --> 00:36:57,200
那我们要不要
瞧瞧你的，那个……
你的“鸡蛋包”？
Shall we have
a look at your, well...
On egg bap?

791
00:36:57,233 --> 00:36:59,667
-噢，那是什么玩意儿？
-押韵俚语。
我寻思拽个词儿。
-Oh, what's that?
-Rhyming slang.
Thought I'd drop it in.

792
00:36:59,700 --> 00:37:01,067
-那是北方俚语吗？
-就是“圈速”。
-Was that a northern one?
-Lap.

793
00:37:01,067 --> 00:37:02,433
圈速啊！噢，懂了，多谢。
Lap! Oh, right. Thank you.

794
00:37:04,100 --> 00:37:06,567
-准备好了吗？放录像吧。
-行，放吧。
-Are we ready? Play the tape.
-Yeah, go on.

795
00:37:06,600 --> 00:37:08,567
（轮胎尖叫声）
(TYRES SCREECHING)

796
00:37:08,600 --> 00:37:10,067
克拉克森：瞧见没？
这一下帅不帅？
CLARKSON: Now, you see?
Was that nice?

797
00:37:10,067 --> 00:37:11,233
温斯顿：还算不赖，是吧？
WINSTONE: It was all right,
wasn't it?

798
00:37:11,267 --> 00:37:12,667
克拉克森：漂亮的烧胎起步。
CLARKSON: Good wheel
spin start.

799
00:37:12,700 --> 00:37:15,100
（引擎轰鸣声）
(ENGINE ROARING)

800
00:37:15,133 --> 00:37:16,933
噢，这架势看着真棒。
Ooh, that's looking good.

801
